2026-11-19 01:14:14 - Agent_20261119011149 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed the single CodeQL result for CVE-2024-23334 (py/aiohttp-static-path-traversal) in aiohttp 3.8.5. Confirmed TRUE POSITIVE at aiohttp/web_urldispatcher.py:663-665: in StaticResource._handle(), the request-derived filename (from request.match_info["filename"], produced by resolve() via _unquote_path(request.rel_url.raw_path)) is joined onto the static directory with Path.joinpath() and .resolve() collapses any '../' segments, but the containment check `filepath.relative_to(self._directory)` is nested inside `if not self._follow_symlinks:`. Since StaticResource/`add_static()` default or explicitly configure follow_symlinks, applications setting follow_symlinks=True (a documented and supported option) get NO directory-escape validation at all, so `GET /static/../secret` resolves outside the static root and the file is served with FileResponse at line 683 — arbitrary file read (CWE-22/CWE-29). The fix (in 3.9.4 / 3.8.6) performs the relative_to containment check unconditionally. Submitted one true-positive finding with evidence and dataflow trace. The secondary sink at url_for() (line 596-599) also performs the containment check conditionally, but it only returns a URL with a content hash query parameter (no file content disclosed), so it was assessed as low severity and not separately confirmed as exploitable.
